<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Museum of Iraq</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1926">1926</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Iraq Museum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The National Museum of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, or Iraq Museum, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> holds one of the world's most important collections of Mesopotamian antiquities from Sumerian, Akkadian, Babylonian and Assyrian sites. Founded from collections assembled under Gertrude Bell in the 1920s, it was looted during the American-led invasion in April 2003; thousands of objects, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warka-vase">Warka Vase</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mask-of-warka">Mask of Warka</a>, were later recovered.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/national-museum-of-iraq.jpg" alt="National Museum of Iraq" width="320" height="201" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hussein A.Al-mukhtar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D8%AA%D8%AD%D9%81_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%88%D8%B7%D9%86%D9%8A_%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B9%D8%B1%D8%A7%D9%82%D9%8A_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
